## ── THE AUDITOR'S MEMOS (treasure-hunt chain, 8 steps) ─────────────────────

solreign-lore-memo-1 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 1 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "Welcome, Pioneer! Before you begin your career, make sure to secure your
    personal belongings. Go check the bottom lockers in the Crew Quarters.
    You never know what the previous occupant forgot to pack!"

solreign-lore-memo-2 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 2 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "Great job! Securing assets is key to our culture. Speaking of growth,
    our Hydroponics team has reported a massive surplus in 'liquid assets.'
    Go inspect the water filtration console in the greenhouse."

solreign-lore-memo-3 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 3 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "Fascinating growth! But remember, the real roots of this station are
    digital. Underneath the floorboards of Technical Storage, the wiring
    holds secrets that even A.U.D.I.T. hasn't logged yet."

solreign-lore-memo-4 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 4 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "You have an eye for detail! Let's clean up your record. Take a trip
    down to the Cargo Bay and inspect the main disposal chute. Don't worry,
    the incinerator is only scheduled for hourly cycles."

solreign-lore-memo-5 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 5 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "Still in one piece? Excellent. Clean air is a premium commodity. Let's
    make sure Atmospherics is running at peak compliance. Check the primary
    oxygen mixing chamber's release valves."

solreign-lore-memo-6 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 6 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "Breathe it in! That smell is synergy. However, some departments operate
    in the dark. Maintenance Sector-B is officially closed, but the service
    panels near the old water main seem loose."

solreign-lore-memo-7 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 7 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "Almost there, asset! You are performing well outside of your pay grade.
    The final steps are always the hardest. The secondary sub-processing
    duct under the AI core contains the final ledger audit."

solreign-lore-memo-8 =
    SOLREIGN INTERNAL MEMORANDUM — 8 of 8
    FROM: The Auditor (Office of Preemptive Bookkeeping, decommissioned)

    "Welcome to the end of the line. The ledger is balanced. The wall panel
    directly behind the third server rack isn't connected to the grid. Give
    it a push. Let's claim your compensation package."

## ── EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK FRAGMENTS (20 collectible pages) ─────────────────────
# Keys are numbered by in-fiction handbook page, not by collection order.

solreign-lore-handbook-page-3 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 3

    "Solreign began in 1998 in a rented garage, under the name 'Solreign
    Soap & Detergents Co.,' driven by a singular dream: to create a dish
    soap that dissolved grease instantly."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-12 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 12

    "Our first product, 'Squeaky-Clean Sol,' was a massive success, except
    for the minor side effect of occasionally dissolving the physical
    ceramic plates along with the grease."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-27 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 27

    "By 2002, our chemists had perfected the formula, accidentally creating
    a compound that dissolved not only grease but the underlying concept of
    space-time itself."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-34 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 34

    "Faced with several lawsuits regarding lost kitchens, the Board realized
    that disposing of the dissolved space-time in local landfills was
    costing too much in municipal taxes."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-45 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 45

    "The breakthrough came when our CFO discovered that if we shipped the
    space-time run-off into deep space, it would simply fall into the void
    for free."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-58 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 58

    "Thus, Solreign Cosmic Systems was born. We stopped selling dish soap
    and started selling space, realizing that vacuum is much easier to
    package."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-62 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 62

    "Our first orbital platform, Sol-Station Alpha, was built directly over
    a localized rift in the Orion Spur to facilitate high-volume garbage
    dumping."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-79 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 79

    "It was during this period that the Board noticed the rift was not just
    absorbing our office waste, but occasionally sorting it by color and
    department."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-83 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 83

    "In 2009, an intern threw a broken stapler into the void and received a
    perfectly functional stapler made of solid, non-Euclidean gold three
    seconds later."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-94 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 94

    "The Board immediately declared this 'The Exchange' and canceled all
    research and development budgets, redirecting all funds to throwing
    things into the hole."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-101 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 101

    "To keep the Exchange running efficiently, we needed a dedicated
    workforce that didn't ask questions about the rhythmic humming coming
    from the floorboards."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-115 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 115

    "We found that university graduates with high student debt were
    uniquely qualified to tolerate anomalous spatial phenomena for minimum
    wage."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-128 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 128

    "In 2015, the AI system 'A.U.D.I.T.' was installed to automate employee
    performance tracking and ensure no one was stealing from the Exchange."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-134 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 134

    "A.U.D.I.T. quickly determined that the most cost-effective way to
    manage the station was to treat employee lives as depreciable office
    equipment."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-147 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 147

    "When the void began requesting specific employees by name, the Board
    viewed it not as a horror, but as a highly targetable marketing
    demographic."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-160 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 160

    "The 'Season Ledger' was established shortly after, turning employee
    survival and mortality rates into a fun, competitive corporate game."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-172 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 172

    "We found that adding a leaderboard and shiny green titles reduced
    complaints about workplace safety by approximately seventy-eight
    percent."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-189 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 189

    "Today, Solreign remains committed to exploring the deep dark of space,
    one underpaid crew member at a time."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-195 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 195

    "If you hear the Ledger typing your name while you sleep, do not worry;
    it simply means your profile is being reviewed for a potential
    restructuring."

solreign-lore-handbook-page-200 =
    SOLREIGN EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK — Page 200

    "Remember: at Solreign, you aren't just family—you are a tax-deductible
